{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Elohim remembered Noah, and every living creature, and all the cattle</b> — The remembrance of Noah was because he was a righteous, wholehearted man, and He had cut a covenant with him to save him; and Noah includes his offspring who were with him there, but He did not mention them explicitly, for it was by his merit that they were saved. But the remembrance that He stated concerning the living creature and the cattle is not on account of merit, for among creatures with a soul there is no merit or liability, except in man alone. Rather, the remembrance of them was because He recalled the word of His holiness that He spoke — that the world should endure — and the will that He had at the creation of the world rose before Him, and He desired the continued existence of the world through the species that He had created in it. And now He saw fit to bring them forth so that they would not perish in the ark. And He did not mention the fowl and the creeping thing, because the remembrance of the living creature is equivalent to theirs, and His friend will declare concerning him:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The final phrase 'ויגיד עליו רעו' (literally 'his friend will declare concerning him') appears to quote Judges 5:11; its precise referent here is uncertain and the translation is hyper-literal."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:26:04.410329339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}